  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">`GraphSubscriptionManager` subscribes to lifecycle notifications and handles `reauthorizationRequired`, `subscriptionRemoved`, and `missed`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A `delta`-query reconciliation backstop runs periodically and feeds missed messages into `IncomingCommunicationProcessor`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Reconciliation is idempotent — a unit test proves a missed message is captured exactly once.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">All Graph calls use central `IGraphClientFactory`; no self-built credential.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Reconciliation failure is non-fatal (NFR-06) — proven by test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`dotnet build` + `dotnet test` green; publish-size delta + CVE result reported; ceiling ≤60 MB respected.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`adr-check` returns no violations against ADR-028 / ADR-010 / ADR-032.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    R-5 mitigation: today only partial polling backup exists. This is the Microsoft-recommended resilience pattern (lifecycle + delta), not a new feature surface.

    BFF-touching: full §10 obligations apply — bff-extensions checklist, Placement Justification, `/conflict-check`, publish-size, CVE.
  </notes>

